WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:14.023
next few days were exciting ones for Cedric.

2
00:00:15.344 --> 00:00:16.465
First, he took Mr.

3
00:00:16.485 --> 00:00:18.266
Havisham to meet the apple seller.

4
00:00:18.286 --> 00:00:24.309
"I have to go to England and be a lord," Cedric explained to the old woman.

5
00:00:24.329 --> 00:00:28.952
"While I'm away, I don't want to worry that you're cold or wet."

6
00:00:30.348 --> 00:00:37.111
Then he told her what he wanted to give her: a tent, a stove, a warm shawl, and

7
00:00:37.271 --> 00:00:38.651
money for rainy days.

8
00:00:41.493 --> 00:00:44.854
The apple seller was so astonished that she almost fell over.

9
00:00:44.874 --> 00:00:49.136
Mr. Havisham and Cedric helped her sit on an empty crate.

10
00:00:49.156 --> 00:00:52.897
"What have I done to deserve this?"

11
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:54.478
she kept repeating.

12
00:00:54.498 --> 00:00:59.060
"You gave me an apple when I hurt my knee," Cedric said.

13
00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.089
"Who could forget that?"

14
00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:05.451
"Many people wouldn't remember," Mr.

15
00:01:05.491 --> 00:01:07.031
Havisham said to himself.

16
00:01:08.572 --> 00:01:10.853
The apple seller smiled up at Cedric.

17
00:01:10.873 --> 00:01:13.654
"You're such a good boy.

18
00:01:13.674 --> 00:01:17.376
I wish I had something to give you in return.

19
00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:19.877
Oh, I know!"

20
00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:22.998
When Cedric and Mr.

21
00:01:23.018 --> 00:01:26.560
Havisham walked away, they each carried a shiny red apple.

22
00:01:28.736 --> 00:01:31.818
Their next stop was the shoeshine stand where Dick worked.

23
00:01:32.938 --> 00:01:35.540
When they arrived, Dick was very upset.

24
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.361
"What's wrong?"

25
00:01:37.841 --> 00:01:38.702
Cedric asked.

26
00:01:38.722 --> 00:01:40.583
"That Jake!

27
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:42.904
I've just been having more trouble with him."

28
00:01:44.025 --> 00:01:47.707
Dick paced in front of the stand, describing their latest argument.

29
00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.189
Cedric was so excited that he could hardly contain himself.

30
00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:53.850
"But, Dick!"

31
00:01:54.271 --> 00:01:56.492
he interrupted when he couldn't wait any longer.

32
00:01:57.292 --> 00:01:59.974
"You don't have to be partners with Jake anymore."

33
00:02:01.935 --> 00:02:02.735
Dick halted.

34
00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.397
"What are you talking about?"

35
00:02:06.658 --> 00:02:11.881
Cedric explained how he'd become a lord, and that his grandfather, the earl, had sent Mr.

36
00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.021
Havisham to New York.

37
00:02:13.041 --> 00:02:18.785
"My grandfather wants me to have anything I want," Cedric said.

38
00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:23.868
"So I decided I want you to have your own shoeshine stand!"

39
00:02:25.264 --> 00:02:28.106
Dick listened to all this with his mouth open.

40
00:02:28.126 --> 00:02:32.049
"Wait just a minute," he finally said.

41
00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:33.971
"You can't fool me.

42
00:02:33.991 --> 00:02:36.332
This is all a joke, right?"

43
00:02:40.896 --> 00:02:41.856
Cedric laughed.

44
00:02:43.117 --> 00:02:44.938
"Nobody believes me at first.

45
00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.861
Mr. Hobbs thought I had sunstroke.

46
00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.823
But I'm telling the truth.

47
00:02:51.343 --> 00:02:51.743
Right, Mr.

48
00:02:53.716 --> 00:02:55.417
Havisham?" "Indeed it's all true."

49
00:02:56.577 --> 00:02:58.478
Mr. Havisham nodded solemnly.

50
00:02:59.719 --> 00:03:03.340
Like the apple seller, Dick had to sit down to absorb the news.

51
00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.662
"Nobody's been this kind to me since my brother, Ben, moved to California.

52
00:03:08.482 --> 00:03:09.723
He always took care of me."

53
00:03:09.743 --> 00:03:12.944
"There's more," Cedric said.

54
00:03:12.964 --> 00:03:17.446
"I'm giving you money for supplies and new clothes too."

55
00:03:19.227 --> 00:03:21.248
Dick stood up and shook Cedric's hand.

56
00:03:22.332 --> 00:03:23.893
"I can't believe my good fortune."

57
00:03:23.913 --> 00:03:27.734
"Well, good-bye, Dick."

58
00:03:28.395 --> 00:03:31.976
Cedric's voice trembled slightly, and he blinked back tears.

59
00:03:31.996 --> 00:03:36.198
"I hope business will be good now that you're on your own.

60
00:03:37.558 --> 00:03:40.940
I hate to leave you, but I have to go to England.

61
00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:45.302
Maybe I'll come back for a visit when I'm an earl."

62
00:03:46.482 --> 00:03:48.463
Cedric fished for something in his pocket.

63
00:03:48.483 --> 00:03:50.804
"Here's my address.

64
00:03:52.448 --> 00:03:53.529
I hope you'll write to me.

65
00:03:54.629 --> 00:03:57.871
But, remember, my name isn't Cedric Errol anymore.

66
00:03:58.872 --> 00:04:00.873
It's Lord Fauntleroy."

67
00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:05.536
Dick took the slip of paper from Cedric and blinked hard.

68
00:04:06.576 --> 00:04:10.138
"I wish you weren't going away," he said in a husky voice.

69
00:04:11.279 --> 00:04:12.800
Then Dick turned to Mr.

70
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:16.282
Havisham. "Thank you, sir, for bringing Cedric to see me.

71
00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:19.864
He's a funny little fellow, but I like him very much."

72
00:04:22.248 --> 00:04:28.331
In a daze Dick watched them leave—a small, eager boy chatting away to a tall, serious man.

73
00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:33.354
"I must do something to thank Cedric," Dick said.

74
00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:39.837
Until the day of his departure, Cedric spent as much time as possible with Mr.

75
00:04:39.857 --> 00:04:45.080
Hobbs. Gloom had settled over Cedric's best friend and his store.

76
00:04:47.121 --> 00:04:50.323
When Cedric brought him a gold watch and chain, Mr.

77
00:04:50.363 --> 00:04:51.804
Hobbs didn't know what to say.

78
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.803
He laid the watch on a counter and blew his nose several times.

79
00:04:56.823 --> 00:05:00.166
"There's something written inside."

80
00:05:01.347 --> 00:05:02.467
Cedric urged Mr.

81
00:05:02.507 --> 00:05:03.809
Hobbs to open the case.

82
00:05:03.829 --> 00:05:07.231
"I told the engraver what to write."

83
00:05:08.492 --> 00:05:10.214
Cedric read the inscription aloud.

84
00:05:11.635 --> 00:05:13.917
From Lord Fauntleroy to Mr.

85
00:05:13.977 --> 00:05:18.000
Hobbs. When this you see, remember me.

86
00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:24.465
"I don't want you to forget me," Cedric explained.

87
00:05:24.485 --> 00:05:27.006
"I won't forget you."

88
00:05:27.606 --> 00:05:30.808
Mr. Hobbs' voice sounded husky, just as Dick's had.

89
00:05:30.828 --> 00:05:36.071
"Don't you forget me when you're among the aristocracy."

90
00:05:36.091 --> 00:05:42.895
"I'll never forget you, no matter who I'm with," Cedric said.

91
00:05:42.915 --> 00:05:46.577
"I've had some of my happiest times with you."

92
00:05:48.738 --> 00:05:51.359
Cedric was sure that his grandfather would invite Mr.

93
00:05:51.399 --> 00:05:52.240
Hobbs to visit.

94
00:05:53.344 --> 00:05:55.985
"You won't mind that he's an earl, will you, Mr.

95
00:05:56.025 --> 00:05:57.846
Hobbs?" Cedric asked.

96
00:05:57.866 --> 00:06:04.329
"I mean, you wouldn't turn down his invitation just because he's an earl?"

97
00:06:04.349 --> 00:06:09.111
"I'll always come to see you," Mr.

98
00:06:09.151 --> 00:06:09.871
Hobbs said.

99
00:06:09.891 --> 00:06:13.053
"Then it's all settled!"

100
00:06:13.493 --> 00:06:14.873
Cedric said cheerfully.

101
00:06:14.893 --> 00:06:20.596
"I'll tell my grandfather all about you and ask him to invite you to his castle!"
